<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Palenque</h1><p class="st-meta">431 CE – 800 CE (approx.) · capital Lakamha' (Palenque)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Classic Maya kingdom of B'aakal in the Chiapas foothills, whose elegant architecture and the tomb of K'inich Janaab Pakal made it one of the best known Maya cities.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Palenque, anciently Lakamha', lies on a ridge above the Gulf lowlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiapas">Chiapas</a>. Its kings counted their dynasty from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuk-bahlam-i">K'uk' B'ahlam I</a>, who took power in 431 CE, and the city grew as the seat of the B'aakal kingdom.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Palenque was sacked twice by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaan">Kingdom of Kaan</a>, in 599 and 611, but recovered under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinich-janaab-pakal">K'inich Janaab Pakal</a>, who reigned from 615 to 683. He built the Palace with its tower and the Temple of the Inscriptions, where his tomb with its carved sarcophagus lid was found in 1952. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinich-kan-bahlam-ii">K'inich Kan B'ahlam II</a> built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cross-group">Cross Group</a>. Palenque was notable for women rulers, its stucco art and long texts.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tonina">Toniná</a> captured the king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kan-joy-chitam-ii">K'an Joy Chitam II</a> in 711, and Palenque declined through the 8th century. The last recorded ruler acceded in 799, and the city was abandoned soon after.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/palenque.jpg" alt="Palenque" width="320" height="637"><figcaption>Image: Ricraider · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palenque_Collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>431 CE – 800 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lakamha' (Palenque)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lady Yohl Ik'nal, K'inich Janaab Pakal, K'inich Kan B'ahlam II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Classic Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>B'aakal, Lakamha', Kingdom of Baakal</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=616&amp;focus=palenque" aria-label="Palenque on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2180 1529 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Palenque lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2500 1785h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2500 1785h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=616&amp;focus=palenque">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

